# Motion & 3D Playbook — Copy-Paste Recipes

Every recipe includes real code, intended use, performance notes, and reduced-motion behavior. Default to `transform` and `opacity`; isolate limited paint-heavy properties such as masks, filters, and color interpolation to short, bounded sequences. Use `will-change` sparingly, lazy-mount heavy layers, and stagger no more than eight items.

## Contents

- **Motion tokens (use these everywhere)**
- **1. Smooth scroll setup (Lenis + GSAP ScrollTrigger)** — React wiring · Vanilla wiring
- **2. 3D scroll effects** — 2a. Perspective card tilt on scroll · 2b. Horizontal pinned section · 2c. Z-depth parallax layers · 2d. Scroll-driven camera dolly · 2e. Page-progress R3F scene
- **3. Hero entrance choreography** — 3a. Staggered word reveal + clip-path mask (GSAP) · 3b. Blur-in entrance (Framer Motion)
- **4. Animated navigation** — 4a. Hide-on-scroll-down glass navbar · 4b. Scroll-progress indicator · 4c. Active-section underline morph · 4d. Mobile menu — 3D flip overlay + staggered links · 4e. Hamburger → X morph (pure CSS/SVG)
- **5. Buttons & micro-interactions** — 5a. Magnetic button (JS) · 5b. Ripple / shine sweep (pure CSS) · 5c. Gradient border spin · 5d. Press physics + success morph (Framer Motion) · 5e. Icon swap on hover (pure CSS)
- **6. Card interactions** — 6a. 3D tilt-on-hover with glare · 6b. Bento hover expansion · 6c. Image zoom + caption reveal
- **7. Scroll reveals** — 7a. Fade-up stagger (IntersectionObserver, framework-free) · 7b. Clip reveal (sections/images) · 7c. Counter animation (stats bands) · 7d. Marquee (logo cloud / ticker)
- **8. Ambient effects** — 8a. Aurora / mesh gradient background (pure CSS) · 8b. Grain overlay (premium texture on dark/gradient heroes) · 8c. Cursor glow follower · 8d. Floating particles (canvas)
- **9. Three.js scroll world (premium tier)** — escalation criteria · quickstart · full playbook pointer
- **10. Particle ambient effects (packaged)** — 10a. Falling leaves · 10b. Pointer trail emitter · 10c. Floating orbs
- **Recipe cheat-sheet**


## Motion tokens (use these everywhere)

```css
:root {
  --dur-micro: 150ms;  /* hover/press (120–200ms) */
  --dur-ui: 300ms;     /* cards, sheets (250–350ms) */
  --dur-hero: 700ms;   /* entrances (500–800ms) */
  --ease-out-expo: cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);   /* default entrance/UI curve */
  --ease-spring: cubic-bezier(0.34, 1.56, 0.64, 1); /* overshoot for playful press */
  --ease-in-out: cubic-bezier(0.65, 0, 0.35, 1);
}
/* Stagger formula: delay = index * 50ms (40–60ms range), max 8 items.
   GSAP: stagger: 0.05 — CSS: transition-delay: calc(var(--i) * 50ms) */
```

Global reduced-motion safety net (include in every project):

```css
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  *, *::before, *::after {
    animation-duration: 0.01ms !important;
    animation-iteration-count: 1 !important;
    transition-duration: 0.01ms !important;
  }
  html { scroll-behavior: auto; }
}
```

---

## 1. Smooth scroll setup (Lenis + GSAP ScrollTrigger)

**When:** a marketing or storytelling surface whose long-form pacing benefits from inertial smoothing. Native scroll is the default for product, utility, accessibility-sensitive, and already well-behaved pages. ScrollTrigger must be synced when Lenis is used.
**Performance:** keep one scroll system, preserve anchors/keyboard behavior, and do not combine Lenis with CSS `scroll-behavior: smooth`.

### React wiring

```bash
npm i lenis gsap
```

```jsx
// hooks/useSmoothScroll.js
import { useEffect } from "react";
import Lenis from "lenis";
import gsap from "gsap";
import { ScrollTrigger } from "gsap/ScrollTrigger";

gsap.registerPlugin(ScrollTrigger);

export function useSmoothScroll() {
  useEffect(() => {
    if (window.matchMedia("(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)").matches) return;

    const lenis = new Lenis({ lerp: 0.1, smoothWheel: true });
    lenis.on("scroll", ScrollTrigger.update);          // keep triggers in sync

    const tick = (time) => lenis.raf(time * 1000);     // gsap ticker drives lenis
    gsap.ticker.add(tick);
    gsap.ticker.lagSmoothing(0);

    return () => {
      gsap.ticker.remove(tick);
      lenis.destroy();
    };
  }, []);
}
```

### Vanilla wiring

```html
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.12.5/dist/gsap.min.js"></script>
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.12.5/dist/ScrollTrigger.min.js"></script>
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/lenis@1.1.14/dist/lenis.min.js"></script>
<script>
  gsap.registerPlugin(ScrollTrigger);
  if (!matchMedia("(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)").matches) {
    const lenis = new Lenis({ lerp: 0.1 });
    lenis.on("scroll", ScrollTrigger.update);
    gsap.ticker.add((t) => lenis.raf(t * 1000));
    gsap.ticker.lagSmoothing(0);
  }
</script>
```

**Reduced-motion fallback:** skip Lenis entirely (native scroll stays).

---

## 2. 3D scroll effects

### 2a. Perspective card tilt on scroll
**When:** hero screenshots, pricing cards — product UI that "rises up" as you scroll into it.
**Performance:** one transform per card; wrap in a `perspective` parent, not `transform-style` chains.

```html
<div class="tilt-stage">
  <div class="tilt-card"><img src="/dashboard.png" alt="Dashboard" /></div>
</div>
<style>
  .tilt-stage { perspective: 1200px; }
  .tilt-card {
    border-radius: 24px; overflow: hidden; box-shadow: var(--shadow-3);
    transform: rotateX(18deg) scale(0.94); transform-origin: center top;
    will-change: transform;
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .tilt-card { transform: none; } }
</style>
<script>
  if (!matchMedia("(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)").matches) {
    gsap.to(".tilt-card", {
      rotateX: 0, scale: 1, ease: "none",
      scrollTrigger: { trigger: ".tilt-stage", start: "top 90%", end: "top 30%", scrub: 0.6 },
    });
  }
</script>
```

### 2b. Horizontal scroll-jacked section
**When:** showcasing 3–5 panels (features, case studies). Pin the section, translate the track horizontally.
**Performance:** translateX on one track only. **Mobile/reduced-motion: degrade to a vertical stack (media query + `ScrollTrigger.matchMedia`).**

```html
<section class="hscroll">
  <div class="hscroll-track">
    <article class="hpanel">…panel 1…</article>
    <article class="hpanel">…panel 2…</article>
    <article class="hpanel">…panel 3…</article>
  </div>
</section>
<style>
  .hscroll { overflow: hidden; }
  .hscroll-track { display: flex; gap: 24px; padding: 0 24px; will-change: transform; }
  .hpanel { flex: 0 0 70vw; max-width: 720px; height: 70vh; border-radius: 24px; }
  @media (max-width: 768px), (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .hscroll-track { flex-direction: column; }
    .hpanel { flex: none; width: 100%; height: auto; }
  }
</style>
<script>
  const mm = gsap.matchMedia();
  mm.add("(min-width: 769px) and (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference)", () => {
    const track = document.querySelector(".hscroll-track");
    gsap.to(track, {
      x: () => -(track.scrollWidth - window.innerWidth),
      ease: "none",
      scrollTrigger: {
        trigger: ".hscroll", pin: true, scrub: 1,
        end: () => "+=" + (track.scrollWidth - window.innerWidth),
        invalidateOnRefresh: true,
      },
    });
  });
</script>
```

### 2c. Z-depth parallax layers (CSS perspective + translateZ)
**When:** hero backgrounds — orbs/blobs/chips floating at different depths. Pure CSS transform, JS-free parallax on scroll is impossible, so pair with a tiny ScrollTrigger scrub or scroll listener.
**Performance:** layers use translateZ (GPU-composited); limit to 3–4 decorative layers; parallax rate 0.2–0.4.

```html
<div class="depth-scene">
  <div class="layer layer-back"></div>   <!-- big blurred orb -->
  <div class="layer layer-mid"></div>    <!-- smaller orb -->
  <div class="layer layer-front"></div>  <!-- chip -->
</div>
<style>
  .depth-scene { position: absolute; inset: 0; perspective: 1000px; overflow: hidden; pointer-events: none; }
  .layer { position: absolute; border-radius: 50%; will-change: transform; }
  .layer-back  { inset: 10% 50% 30% -10%; background: radial-gradient(circle, var(--accent) 0%, transparent 70%); opacity: .25; filter: blur(60px); transform: translateZ(-300px) scale(1.4); }
  .layer-mid   { inset: 40% -5% 10% 60%; background: radial-gradient(circle, #8B5CF6 0%, transparent 70%); opacity: .2; filter: blur(50px); transform: translateZ(-150px) scale(1.2); }
  .layer-front { width: 120px; height: 120px; right: 12%; top: 20%; background: var(--glass, rgba(255,255,255,.1)); backdrop-filter: blur(12px); border-radius: 24px; transform: translateZ(60px); }
</style>
<script>
  if (!matchMedia("(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)").matches) {
    gsap.to(".layer-back",  { yPercent: 20, ease: "none", scrollTrigger: { trigger: ".depth-scene", start: "top top", end: "bottom top", scrub: true } });
    gsap.to(".layer-mid",   { yPercent: 35, ease: "none", scrollTrigger: { trigger: ".depth-scene", start: "top top", end: "bottom top", scrub: true } });
